# This is not a standalone unit definition. MariaDB's real systemd unit
# (mariadb.service) is owned and upgraded by the mariadb-server package, so
# forking it here would drift out of sync. install.sh instead symlinks
# /etc/systemd/system/hiddify-mysql.service straight to the installed
# mariadb.service unit — the same alias mechanism the package itself uses
# for mysql.service — so systemctl operations on "hiddify-mysql" act on the
# real MariaDB service.
#
# This file exists so scripts/restart.sh and scripts/status.sh, which
# discover services via `services/**/*.service`, pick up "hiddify-mysql"
# like every other service.
